      {
        "id": 121168,
        "name": "Foote",
        "username": "Foote",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-12-09T21:05:22.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"phantaskippy\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/48/1897_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> phantaskippy:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I like Operative vs. Blade a lot, pull him away from your allies, or bitter spiral to double up on his redistributor. &nbsp;Either way it is fun to be able to just focus him down. &nbsp;(Poisons are also really good vs. Baron)</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Agreed. Anytime you can debuff Blade is going to be huge. Make all his attacks melee so you take away his biggest weapon, the arm cannon. You force him into his armor suit, but then he can't teleport effectivly due to the push. Making him one dimensional instead of multi-faceted is a great strat against him.</p>",
